                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tuberous mass of cells that is the embryonic form of orchids and club mosses"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c63cb11-555c-43c4-8180-be1cb1a35203",
                                                "sense_id": "e94c1502-3aeb-310f-8be1-2eec191f0953",
                                                "text": "Orchids rely on fungi to reproduce. Their tiny seeds don't have any on-board nutrients (like beans and apples) and will not germinate until they are infected by a symbiotic fungus which supplies them with food. Known as a protocorm, this tiny orchid-fungus ball grows, turns green and eventually starts to photosynthesise."
                                            }
